  "interpretation": [
    "The two expanded native Qt attempts retain eight preceding stopped/moving cases but do not receive the complete new background entry. Passing prefixes are not added to #344 acceptance.",
    "First minimized save has a real new native draw, but document visibility becomes visible during the operation; it is not proof of continuous hidden capture.",
    "The next attempted session save reaches the original five-second deadline, preserves the caller destination and drains capture registries. Its surface-restoration oracle then fails.",
    "A no-Viewer/no-WebEngine QWidget control also does not retain the requested minimized state at its observation. This does not establish a Viewer product defect or a universal Qt defect.",
    "Separate headless and headed Chromium controls keep document.visibilityState visible after switching real tabs, even after requesting focus-emulation disable on auxiliary CDP sessions and removing three default background flags. A later control identifies the same native window for both tabs and also requests native minimization; visibility still stays visible. These driver observations do not qualify true background scheduling.",
    "Playwright source enables focus emulation on its owning main-frame CDP session. An auxiliary-session disable has not established native visibility behavior; no installed dependency is patched.",
    "No DOM visibility getter, scientific reply, native glyph result or elapsed deadline is fabricated.",
    "All six campaigns are bounded, keep fixed selected inputs, retain originals and close every owned process.",
    "No new product correction or source capability advertisement is selected from these inconclusive host controls."
  ],
  "next": [
    "Use a receiving driver that can demonstrably observe genuine native background/foreground transitions before receiving saves; do not repeat the same unqualified switching recipe.",
    "Isolate compositor activation/exposure from scene transport; ordinary native restoration and any explicit remapping route keep distinct acceptance.",
    "Keep the complete #344 actual-host source receiving and proceed with independently actionable robustness work while this host-control boundary is resolved."
  ],
